course: dictionary
lesson: 3549
title: Many meanings of one word
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: The word feeling has more than one meaning, so context tells you which one to pick. Most often it means an emotion, such as happy, sad, angry or scared. «Anger is a normal feeling, but it makes the body ready to fight.» Here feeling means an emotion that everyone can have.
explain: Sometimes feeling is about your body. «I have no feeling in my fingers» means you cannot sense touch there. Feelings can also mean someone's emotions that can be hurt. «The kind words protect feelings» shows that kindness looks after people's hurt emotions.
explain: To choose the right meaning, ask: is this about the body, an emotion, a guess, or someone's heart? Then swap your meaning into the sentence. If it still makes sense, you have found it.
fact: Feeling is a noun (feeling, feelings), the -ing form of the verb feel, and an adjective meaning showing emotions.
fact: «Feeling» can mean an emotion, such as happy, sad, angry or scared.
fact: «Feeling» can mean something in your body, like «a feeling of cold».
fact: «Feeling» can mean an idea that is not sure, like «I have a feeling it will rain».
fact: «Feelings» can mean someone's emotions that can be hurt, as in «hurt her feelings».
exercise: «Anger is a normal feeling, but it makes the body ready to fight.» What does feeling mean here? | *An emotion, such as anger | A map of the town | A loud noise | A cold drink
exercise: Ella says, «I have a feeling it will rain.» What does feeling mean? | The hurt inside someone | *An idea that is not sure | Touch in her fingers | An emotion, like happy
exercise: «The kind words protect feelings, but you still need to know what really happened.» What are feelings here? | Shapes on paper | The weather | *Someone's emotions that can be hurt | Something you hear
test: «I have no feeling in my fingers.» What does feeling mean? | *The ability to feel with touch | An idea that is not sure | A fast heartbeat | An emotion, like sad
test: Which of these is the -ing form of the verb feel? | feeler | *feeling | feels | felt
exam: Which meaning fits in «Some apps use pretend feelings, like a sad AI friend»? | Touch in the fingers | An idea that is not sure | A hot, sweaty day | *An emotion, such as sad
